// REJECTS: Unexpected token '='. Valid alternatives: ['.']
//
// A tagged value is always `<profilePath>.<tag> = <value>`. The profile qualifier is not
// optional and there is no "current profile" to elide it against.
//
// The parser demands '.' rather than reporting a missing profile, which is the behaviour
// to match: the qualified name is parsed as ONE path expression, not as an optional prefix
// on a tag name. A rewrite that models it as `tag (':' profile)?` or that resolves a bare
// tag against imports accepts this, and the resulting protocol carries a tagged value
// whose profile is null.
###Pure
Class {doc = 'unqualified tag'} fixture::neg::BareTag
{
   code: String[1];
}
